      "Turn-flow example: Red 3s: placed face up before play, replaced with new cards. Opening (team's first meld): Can only be done at START of turn before drawing. Requirements: 50+ pts if team score <3000; 90+ pts if 3000-5000; 120+ pts if >5000. Opening player continues with normal turn. Before opening: draw 2 from stock, meld any red 3s drawn (replaced), discard 1 to end turn. After opening: draw either (a) 2 from stock, OR (b) entire discard pile + 1 from stock. Then may meld, then discard. Melds: 3+ cards same rank. Natural melds: max 2 wild cards (must have more naturals than wilds). Canasta: 7+ card meld. Clean (pulito): no wilds. Dirty (sporco): has wilds. Wild card meld: commits team to complete 7+ wild canasta; cannot use wilds elsewhere until completed. Special canastas: Wild canasta clean = all 2s or all 6 jokers+1 two; dirty = 1-5 jokers+2s. Ace canasta: 7+ aces. Threes: red 3s score separately; black 3s can only be discarded, never melded. Frozen pile: if has wild or black 3 on top, can only take if have 2 natural cards of same rank as top card in hand.",
      'Scoring example: When the play ends, each team scores positive points for the cards they have melded and negative points for any cards remaining in their hands. When the play ends, each team scores positive points for the cards they have melded and negative points for any cards remaining in their hands..',
